{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175176": {
      "title": "FA26-016: Lecturer Open Recruitment for Spring 2026, AY2026-2027 and Summer 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-10-02 Location: Edwardsville, IL Periodically, the College of Arts and Sciences may have openings throughout the year (Summer 2026, AY2026-2027 and Summer 2027) for various part-time, non-tenure, semester term lecturer appointments. These openings may occur in any of the following College of Arts and Sciences departments/programs: Anthropology, Applied Communication Studies, Art and Design, Art Therapy, Biological Sciences, Chemistry, Criminal Justice Studies, English Language and Literature, Environmental Sciences, Foreign Languages and Literature, Forensic Sciences MS, Geography and GIS, History, Mass Communications, Mathematics and Statistics, Music, Philosophy, Political Science, Public Administration and Policy Analysis (PAPA), Social Work, Sociology, Theater and Dance, Black Studies, as well as Women's, Gender, and Sexuality Studies. For more information on specific departments or the College of Arts & Sciences, please visit: https://www.siue.edu/arts-and-sciences/ Southern Illinois University Edwardsville nurtures an open, respectful, and welcoming climate that facilitates learning and work. SIUE is committed to education that explores the historic significance of diversity in order to understand the present and to better enable our community to engage the future. Integral to this commitment, Southern Illinois University Edwardsville strives for a student body and a workforce that is both diverse and inclusive. Terms of Appointment Varies Source of Funds State Salary Table of Salaries Per Class Lecturer Rates Department Anthropology Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Applied Communications Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Art & Design Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Art Therapy Masters  5,000.00     PhD  5,000.00 Biological Sciences Masters  4,615.02     PhD  5,076.52 Chemistry Masters  3,822.34     PhD  4,204.57 Criminal Justice Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,965.50 English Language & Literature Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Environmental Sciences Masters  4,521.76     PhD  4,521.76 Foreign Languages & Literature Masters  4,145.75     PhD  4,145.75 Forensic Science Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Geography & GIS Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 History Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,965.50 Mass Communications Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Mathematics & Statistics Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Music Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Philosophy Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,965.50 Political Science Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 PAPA Masters  4,195.36     PhD  4,195.36 Sociology Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,965.50 Social Work Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Theater & Dance Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Black Studies Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Women's Gender, and Sexuality Studies Masters  3,605.00     PhD  3,605.00 Note: All are based on 3 credit hour courses or 20% except Foreign Languages & Literature which is based on 23% because of built in labs. An advanced degree in discipline of instruction (or equivalent professional experience in Fine Arts) is required. Submit cover letter, resume, and transcripts for the following departments/programs: Anthropology, Applied Communication Studies, Art and Design, Art Therapy, Biological Sciences, Chemistry, Criminal Justice Studies, English Language and Literature, Environmental Sciences, Foreign Languages and Literature, Forensic Sciences MS, Geography and GIS, History, Mass Communications, Mathematics and Statistics, Music, Philosophy, Political Science, Public Administration and Policy Analysis, Social Work, Sociology, and Theater and Dance, Black Studies, as well as Women’s Studies, Gender, and Sexuality Studies. For more information on each department or to search for specific contacts, visit the CAS home page at: https://www.siue.edu/arts-and-sciences/ Application Deadline The departments will accept applications throughout the year and will continue to review applications on an ongoing basis based on position availability. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "College of Arts and Sciences"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179156": {
      "title": "FA26-030: Assistant Professor in Painting and Digital Illustration",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-16 Location: Edwardsville, IL The Department of Art and Design at Southern Illinois University Edwardsville (SIUE) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor specializing in Painting and Digital Illustration, beginning August 2026. We seek candidates with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentorship, a strong exhibition record, and an active creative practice. The successful candidate will teach a range of courses-from foundations to advanced levels-in painting and digital illustration for both undergraduate and graduate students. They will collaborate with current drawing and painting faculty to strengthen the existing painting curriculum and will develop new coursework and curricular pathways in digital illustration. Additional responsibilities include student mentorship and advising, participation in MFA thesis committees, and service to the department, college, and university. The Department of Art and Design The NASAD-accredited Department of Art and Design includes 17 full-time faculty and offers undergraduate degrees in Art History, Art Studio, and Art Education, as well as graduate degrees in Art Studio and Art Therapy. The department is housed in a renovated, state-of-the-art facility on the main SIUE campus, featuring a 3,700-square-foot gallery, two dedicated smart classrooms for art history, and generously equipped studios supporting concentrations in: art education, ceramics, photography/digital arts, sculpture, glass, textiles, metalworking/jewelry, graphic design, painting, drawing, and printmaking. The department hosts multiple exhibitions each year and supports a robust visiting artist and scholar program. Faculty also have access to the Louis Su l livan Ornament Collection-the world's largest known collection of the architect's ornamental work and salvaged architectural pieces-and the SIUE University Museum, an archive and research center housing more than 35,000 objects from archaeological artifacts to natural science specimens to fine art. Terms of Appointment Academic term, 9-month Source of Funds State MFA in Studio Art with concentration in Painting Demonstrated specialization in digital illustration Demonstrated skills at painting from direct observation At least two years of college-level teaching experience Active exhibition record Preferred Qualifications Global vision for developing a curriclulum in contemporary art Commitment to developing a curriculum that exposes students to multiple cultural forms and diverse perspectives Deep understanding of art theory Evidence of working collaboratively with colleagues across disciplines Experience with, and commitment to, educating and mentoring students of diverse backgrounds and demographics Submit a cover letter outlining interest in and qualifications for the position, curriculum vita, statement of teaching philosophy, representative syllabi, portfolio of 20 professional artworks and 20 samples of student work (with image list), official transcript for highest degree completed, and names and contact information for three professional references. Please address questions about the position to Professor Brigham Dimick, Search Committee Chair (bdimick@siue.edu). This institution is using lnterfolio's Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. SIUE nurtures an open, respectful, and welcoming climate that facilitates learning and work. SIUE is committed to education that explores the historic significance of diversity in order to understand the present and to better enable our community to engage the future. Integral to this commitment, SIUE strives for a student body and a workforce that is both diverse and inclusive. Candidates from historically underrepresented groups, including women, members of racially minoritized groups, and individuals with disabilities, are strongly encouraged to apply. To learn more about the Department of Art and Design's contributions to the University's core values of diversity, equity, and inclusion: Art and Design Department Mission Statement. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "College of Arts and Sciences"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171421": {
      "title": "FA26-002: Asst Prof/Assoc Prof/Prof or Clin Asst Prof/Clin Assoc Prof/Clin Prof (depending on qualifications)",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-08-14 Location: Alton, IL The Southern Illinois University School of Dental Medicine is seeking applications for a full-time tenure track position at the Assistant/Associate Professor level in the Department of Surgical Sciences and Community Care, Section of Periodontology. Responsibilities include teaching in the pre-doctoral program, as well as independent research and service to the University. Working in collaboration with other faculty, both in research and in teaching, is encouraged. Source of Funds State Salary Assistant Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor: $120,000-$145,000 Associate Professor/Clinical Associate Professor: $130,000-$155,000 Professor/Clinical Professor: $140,000-$165,000 A D.M.D. or D.D.S degree and specialty training in Periodontics from a CODA accredited postgraduate program, or foreign equivalent, in periodontics and American Board of Periodontology eligibility or certification are required. Previous teaching experience and/or a record of research accomplishments through publication and external funding are desirable. Candidates holding an M.S. degree are preferred. Applicants must be licensed to practice dentistry in the state of Illinois, or be able to meet the requirements for Illinois licensure. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Intramural faculty practice is available. Submit letter of application, resume, transcripts, and references. Application Deadline The position will remain open until filled. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Dental Medicine"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173155": {
      "title": "FA26-013: Assistant/Associate Professor / Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (depending on qualifications)",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-09-03 Location: Alton, IL The Southern Illinois University School of Dental Medicine is seeking applications for a full-time tenure track or clinical track position at the Assistant/Associate Professor / Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor level in the Department of Clinical Practice & Operative Dentistry. Responsibilities include didactic, pre-clinical, and clinical teaching. For tenure-track appointments, independent research, scholarly activities and service to the University are also expected. Excellence in teaching is integral to the mission of Southern Illinois University and the School of Dental Medicine. Source of Funds State Term of Contract Dependent on rank Salary - Commensurate with Qualifications Asst Prof/Clin Asst Prof: $120,000-$130,000 Assoc Prof/Clin Assoc Prof: $130,00-$140,000 Prof/Clin Prof: $140,000-$150,000 A D.M.D. or D.D.S. degree from a CODA accredited dental school or international equivalent. Candidates should demonstrate an interest in teaching pre-doctoral students in General Dentistry. Advanced Education in General Dentistry training is desirable. Experience in evidence-based teaching and dental material sciences is also highly desirable. Applicants must be able to meet the requirements to obtain a dental license or a restricted faculty license in Illinois. Opportunity for extramural faculty practice is available. Submit letter of intent, curriculum vitae, and three letters of references. Application Deadline Review of applications will begin upon receipt and continue until the position is filled. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Dental Medicine"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172030": {
      "title": "FA26-010: Lecturer, Continuing Open Recruitment for AY2025-2026 and Summer 2026",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-08-14 Location: Edwardsville, IL The SIUE School of Engineering is accepting resume packages for various part-time, non-tenure, semester term lecturer appointments for the 2025-2026 academic year. This listing does not represent an actual vacancy; rather open recruitment allows interested persons to submit materials for future vacancies within the School of Engineering.  These non-tenure track faculty positions may occur in any of the following School of Engineering departments: Civil Engineering, Computer Science, Construction, Electrical & Computer Engineering, Industrial Engineering, and Mechanical Engineering. For more information regarding the School of Engineering and the various departments within, please visit: https://www.siue.edu/engineering/ Source of Funds State Terms of Appointment Academic, non-tenure, term, percent of appointment varies. Salary Degree Years of Experience Course Enrollment New Pay Rate MS            0-5                                  50 or less                     $4,000.00 MS            5-10                                50 or less                     $4,250.00 MS            10-15                              50 or less                     $4,500.00 MS            >15                                 50 or less                     $4,750.00 PhD           0-5                                 50 or less                     $4,850.00 PhD           5-10                               50 or less                     $5,150.00 PhD           10-15                             50 or less                     $5,250.00 PhD           >15                                50 or less                     $5,500.00 Advanced degree in the relevant discipline or equivalent experience is required. Proficiency in course content and fluency in the English language are required for appointment carrying teaching responsibilities. Submit a letter of application, resume, curriculum vitae, transcripts, and three professional letters of reference. Application Deadline The departments will accept applications throughout the year and will continue to review applications based on position availability and departmental need. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Engineering"
