      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12 Deadline: 2026-11-06 Location: Edwardsville, Il Hiring Unit School of Education, Health, and Human Behavior, Department of Psychology Position Title Instructor - Psychology Job Description/Responsibilities Southern Illinois University Edwardsville’s School of Education, Health, and Human Behavior is seeking qualified applicants for an Instructor-Psychology position. Preferred applicants will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching, with an emphasis on both on-ground and online instruction. The successful applicant will contribute to our growing undergraduate program through the development and teaching of program courses. Teaching responsibilities are four classes per semester, with possible opportunities for summer teaching. Full-time instructors are also required to maintain a \"fifth-unit\" of responsibility, which is negotiated with the Department Chair. To learn more about the department, visit us online at: https://www.siue.edu/education/psychology/ The Department of Psychology seeks to attract an active, culturally and academically diverse faculty. SIUE is committed to diversity to achieve domestic and international peace, social justice, and the development of full human potential. Integral to this commitment, the School of Education, Health, and Human Behavior strives for a student body and a workforce that manifests diversity.  Applicants who embody diversity of race, color, creed or religion, age, sex, national origin, disability, sexual orientation, or sexual identity are encouraged to apply. Terms of Appointment Full-time, continuing 9-month non-tenure-track instructor position. Summer appointment is contingent upon availability of funds and enrollment.  Beginning date of appointment is August 2027. Source of funds State For more information about employment benefits and policies, visit: Faculty Employment Benefits Minimum Qualifications Applicants for this position must possess a Master’s degree in Psychology or Doctoral degree in Psychology by the contract start date in August 2027. Preferred Qualifications Ability to teach undergraduate courses in areas of expertise and departmental need including, for example, Foundations of Psychology, Theories of Personality, Statistics and Research Methods, Multicultural Psychology, and Careers in Psychology. Actual course assignments may vary depending on departmental need. Ability and interest to on-ground as well as online-asynchronous courses. Demonstrated interest in teaching and working with students from diverse backgrounds. Commitment to departmental and university collegiality through a \"fifth-unit\" service-related activity. SIUE is committed to diversity and inclusivity and seeks candidates who can contribute, through their interest, teaching, or service, to the diversity and excellence of the academic community. Application Process Please submit a letter of application which includes contact information for three references, vitae, and academic transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable). Material should be submitted electronically alongside the application. Questions about the position can be directed to Dr. Dan Segrist, Search Chair, dsegris@siue.edu Application Deadline For optimal consideration in a first pool of applicants, all application materials must be received by the end of the business day on November 6th, 2026.  A second pool of applicants may be reviewed after this date if the position is not filled from the first pool of applicants. Southern Illinois University Edwardsville is a premier metropolitan university located on the bluffs of the Mississippi River just 22 miles east of St. Louis, MO.  SIUE offers over 12,000 culturally diverse students and a wide range of undergraduate and graduate degree programs. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  