    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195605": {
      "title": "FA27-035: Assistant/Associate Professor or Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13 Location: Alton, Il The Southern Illinois University School of Dental Medicine is seeking applications for a full-time tenure or clinical track position at the Assistant/Associate Professor level in the Department of Prosthodontics and Endodontics. Responsibilities include didactic and clinical teaching in the pre-doctoral program, with an emphasis on Removable & Fixed Prosthodontics, and service to the University. As programs expand, participation in graduate education while helping advance the department's mission through innovation, collaboration, and academic excellence. For tenure-track appointments, independent research and scholarly activity is also expected. Working in collaboration with other faculty, both in research and teaching, is strongly encouraged. Extramural/intramural faculty practice is available. Salary Asst Prof/Clin Asst Prof: $120,000 to $145,000 Assoc Prof/Clin Assoc Prof: $130,000 to $155,000 Prof/Clin Prof: $140,000 to $165,000 Source of Funds State Qualifications A D.M.D. or D.D.S. degree (or foreign equivalent) is required. Specialty training in prosthodontics from a CODA accredited postgraduate program is preferred. Candidates who are board certified or board eligible by the American Board of Prosthodontics are preferred. Candidates holding an MS degree are preferred. Demonstrated interest and experience in teaching and research are desired. Applicants must be licensed to practice dentistry in the state of Illinois, or be able to meet the requirements for Illinois licensure. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. SUBMIT LETTER OF INTENT, CV, AND THREE LETTERS OF REFERENCE ALONGSIDE THE APPLICATION IN INTERFOLIO. Application Deadline The position will remain open until filled. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu.",
